From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:09:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 095/148] hjviewer: ask once before a link connects, without
 its password (TV-C6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-C6 (Dart; D-13, critic 2-7, X-17, X-18): a pinned server build,
known by allow-deep-link-password pinned to N (no new core key, no
bridge change), takes links only as hjviewer:// or rustdesk:// (both in
1.9.0), drops a link's password (?password= and --password), so that
the PC asks, and asks LK1 "PC {ID}에 연결할까요?" [취소] [연결] once
before a link opens a connection: on a desktop in handleUriLink, which
brings the main window up for it, for links and --connect alike; on a
phone in urlLinkToCmdArgs. A phone where A0 comes anyway skips LK1 and
A0 carries LK1's line with the PC's ID instead. [연결] handles the same
link once more, unasked; [취소] or no overlay within five seconds opens
nothing. Builds that are not pinned keep upstream's links.

handleUriLink first hands all three of its inputs to hjvHandleGateLink:
any hjviewer://hjv-gate link is taken before the scheme filter, and only
/login and /password without a query open something, on Windows only
(the login, or P2 while P1 shows), for the tray's items (UX-G2). A phone,
which any web page can hand such a link, opens nothing.

A QR code read from an image is a link with either scheme.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
